This allows specifying visibility at impl-level. For example:

```rust
// unnamed
#[ext(pub)]
impl str {
    fn foo(&self) {}
}

// named
#[ext(pub StrExt)]
impl str {
    fn bar(&self) {}
}
```

associated-item-level visibility will continue to be supported. Note that you cannot specify impl-level visibility and associated-item-level visibility at the same time.

```rust
// unnamed
#[ext(pub)]
impl str {
    pub fn foo(&self) {} //~ ERROR all associated items must have inherited visibility
}
```

